// Official auto-attack hit feedback tables for RO-Next.
//
// Generated by `tools/gen_hit_feedback.py`; do not edit by hand.
// Regenerate with: `./tools/gen_hit_feedback.py`
// Drift check:      `./tools/gen_hit_feedback.py --check`
//
// Sources (committed facts, no game files needed to regenerate):
//   * CondaRO client archive CondaRO.grf: data\luafiles514\lua files\datainfo\weapontable.lub (plain Lua, EUC-KR)
//     table `WeaponHitWaveNameTable + Weapon_IDs`; logic Source/Contents/Sound/HitSounds.cpp:34-77 (CSession::GetWeaponHitWaveName), Source/Client/Session/Session.cpp:3526-3537 (InitWeaponHitWaveNames default "_hit_mace.wav" for all 105 slots).
//     CondaRO.grf is the patch archive whose table names match the data\wav files that exist; the compiled data.grf copy names _hit_소총/_hit_개틀링건/_hit_유탄발사기.wav for the three gun classes, which are not shipped in either archive.
//   * Source/Contents/Sound/HitSounds.cpp InitJobHitWaveNames (CondaRO client decompilation) (`78`).
//     140 explicit rows; unlisted jobs use player_clothes.wav (HitSounds.cpp:107-108). GetHitWaveName (HitSounds.cpp:15-32) indexes jobs > 3950 with index = job - 3950.
//   * Source/Contents/Actors/RenderObject.cpp CGameActor::ProcessHitMessage (CondaRO client decompilation): RenderObject.cpp:3800-3822 selects effectId: EF_HIT1 (0) normally, EF_HITLINE7 (434) for the Taekwon/Star job family and EF_VIOLEN_HIT (2420) for Violen. RenderObject.cpp:3769-3782 sets hitEffect (EF_HIT2, 1) only for a critical hit.
//     effect ids: Source/Contents/Effects/Core/EffectTypes.h:8 (EF_HIT1 = 0), :9 (EF_HIT2 = 1), :442 (EF_HITLINE7 = 434), :2428 (EF_VIOLEN_HIT = 2420).
//     job ids: Source/Contents/Jobs/JobId.h:3412-3610, :3647-3661 (JT_TAEKWON=4046 .. JT_SKY_EMPEROR2=4316), :4040-4041 (JT_VIOLEN=22383, JT_CP_VIOLEN=22384).
//
// `weapon_waves` is indexed by the client `WeaponKind`; the official
// `GetWeaponHitWaveName(-1)` (no attacker weapon) and `realWeapon == 0`
// (bare hand, non-Taekwon) branches are the two random `*_waves` lists.
// `job_waves` is the defender's clothing impact wave; jobs above 3950 use
// `index = job - 3950`, every unlisted job uses `job_default_wave`.
(
    provenance: "CondaRO client weapontable.lub + client decompilation; generated by tools/gen_hit_feedback.py",
    version: 2,
    // Official `WeaponHitWaveNameTable`, one row per `WeaponKind`.
    weapon_waves: [
        (kind: Fist, wave: "_hit_mace.wav"),
